Explain the exercise’s control architecture in terms of the paradigms explained on the lecture slides, i.e., 
sense-think-act, reactivity, behaviors, subsumption, etc.

Well predefined set of actions, which are thought through before the execution happens.

- In our exercise here predefined actions could be following the given trajectory.
Initially we are given the circle trajectory and then the end-effector will follow that.
Also following the line/ellipse trajectory is predefined as the end effector follows
the predefined trajectory.

Sense-think-act logic:

- parameter for enabling/disabling feedforward control. On the update function
we are continuously checking whether to use this ff_ctrl or not.
So here the joint_ctrl.cpp is sensing the current joint states from the hardware
interfaces and comparing them with the desired trajectory. When the user sets
use_feedforward to true/false then we will act based on enabling/disabling the feedforward controller.
This makes the controller's think-step configurable.

- changing trajectory is based on callback for continuous sending of messages. So via user
commands we can change the sensed trajectory. The architecture then computes the
error between the current state and the desired trajectory and acts based on that so that the desired
trajectory is achieved.

- We are  sensing the current joint states from hardware interfaces and
computing the error between current states and desired trajectory and acting based on that.

- So all in all, this architecture has both predefined and sense-think-act actions
so I would personally say that this would land in the world of hybrid control
architectures as we have predefined actions but we can alter that via user commands
and act on sensed things such as changing parameters and computing the error to
decide what action to take.

Conclusions of the control architecture:

Trajectory publisher:
	- No environmental sensing, but changing trajectory parameter could be interpreted as:
		○ Sense: Detect a parameter change. Configuration monitoring, no environmental sensing
		○ Think: Select trajectory generation function. No thinking/planning, 
		more like deterministic decision logic inside the node
		○ Act: Generate and publish selected trajectory
	- Trajectories can be changed at runtime -> Control logic itself remains the same but it starts 
	tracking different trajectory
	- No priority-based behaviors so there is no subsumption
	- No world model or planning
	- Single competence: generate and publish trajectory joint positions and velocities

Joint controller:
	- Control logic can be interpreted as a sense-think-act loop:
		○ Sense: desired joint positions, current joint positions
		○ Think: compute the control input inside joint controller's update() method 
		○ Act: send velocity commands to the command interface
	- Think-step is limited to error computation and a reconfigurable control law, with no world model or planning
	- Control command is a direct function of the current joint state and the current reference but it can be altered 
	by changing whether it is using the feedforward 
	term -> reconfiguring the control logic to use desired velocities as an additional control input
	- Single competence: tracking the trajectory provided by the trajectory publisher